course: dictionary
lesson: 16010
title: Variegated: many colours at once
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Variegated is a long word, but the words around it give clues. «The variegated ivy had green leaves edged with cream.» The words green and cream are colours, and edged tells you the colours are on the edges. So variegated must mean having patches or edges of different colours.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The ivy had green leaves edged with patches of different colours.» It still makes sense, so you are right. A plain green meaning would not fit, because the sentence names more than one colour.
explain: Variegated can describe other things too, not just plants. «Her blanket was variegated, with red, blue and yellow squares.» The list of colours is the clue, so here it means full of many different colours or kinds.
fact: Variegated means having patches, stripes or edges of different colours.
fact: Gardeners often use it for plants such as ivy, whose leaves may be green and white or green and yellow.
fact: Variegated can also mean having many different colours or kinds, like a variegated stone or a variegated yarn.
fact: Variegated is a longer word for something you might call "many colours", so the clues around it help you check.
fact: To test a new word, say its meaning in your own words, then read the sentence again to see if it fits.
exercise: «The variegated ivy had green leaves edged with cream.» What does variegated mean here? | Plain and all one colour | Covered in snow | Very old and tall | *Patches or edges of different colours
exercise: Ella says variegated means very green. Why is she wrong? | Variegated means very tall | *Variegated leaves can have white or yellow too, so it means more than green | Variegated means very green, so she is right | Variegated means having many colours or kinds, not just one colour
exercise: «Her sweater was a variegated mix of red, blue and yellow.» What does this tell you? | Her sweater was very old | *Her sweater had many different colours | Her sweater was wet through | Her sweater was one plain colour
test: «The gardener bought a variegated plant with yellow edges on its leaves.» What is variegated in this sentence? | Full of water | Tall and thin | Very cheap | *Patches of different colours
test: Which kind of leaf is variegated? | Brown dead leaves | *Green leaves with white or yellow edges | Plain green leaves | Leaves with no colour at all
exam: Which sentence uses variegated correctly? | He variegated his sandwich at lunch | *The variegated ivy had green and cream leaves | The variegated bus was very quiet | The variegated sky was dark and plain
